Usage:
  commons <command> [options] [--json]

Store:
  init                 create a store in a directory (default: the working
                       directory)
  status               store recovery state, unfinished operations and the
                       durability declaration
  fsck                 check the store: blobs re-hashed, statements re-read,
                       references resolved, journal and cache checked
  repair               finish committed operations the store could not finish:
                       reinstall, re-check blobs, rebuild projections
  gc                   list (default) or delete unreferenced blobs outside the
                       grace window; release a blob this store serves
  history              list operations this store finished, newest first (local,
                       not authoritative)

Read:
  list                 every blob a statement in this store names, and every
                       resource, one line of tokens each
  show                 show a blob (authorship, grade, every disclosure), a
                       statement, a resource, or a key
  explain              the statements, policy, evaluator and time context behind
                       every token shown
  verify               check a blob or a statement from the statements held;
                       exit per the exit table

Publish and keys:
  publish              sign and commit a statement (authored with its bytes,
                       holds, describes, retracts, or a draft)
  publish task         create a task (genesis + first edition) or publish a new
                       edition of one
  publish grant        sign a task coordinator's grant for one edition
  key new              generate a signing key into a new file (mode 0600, never
                       overwritten)
  key show             print the signer and algorithm of a key file (never the
                       key), or of a Ledger device's key
  key sign             sign an external-signing package's PAE bytes with a key
                       file (reads no store)
  package show         check an external-signing package and print what its
                       signature would cover (reads no store)
  rotate               rotate your signing key: sign a rotate_key naming its
                       successor
  revoke               revoke your signing key: sign a revoke_key whose history
                       keeps what you choose

Identity:
  identity new         create a fixed-root identity: sign its inception with a
                       fresh root key
  identity grant       grant a delegate key the right to act for an identity
  identity cut         cut a grant: the delegate's acts after --last-good stop
                       counting for the identity

Exchange:
  pull                 admit a package (a store tree in a directory or a tar
                       archive) into this store under this reader's policy
  push                 judge the commits of this hub checkout as the hub's CI
                       would, apply the anchor and withheld-bytes preconditions,
                       and when all is clean git push the judged commit (never
                       forced; --dry-run sends nothing)
  fetch                obtain blobs from the locations held `holds` statements
                       name, verified by full hash; never publishes a holds
  hub check            check a change to the hub this directory is in, as the
                       hub's CI does (writes nothing)

Run:
  run                  run a held workflow under your execution policy;
                       --publish signs what it emits

Anchors:
  anchor stamp         timestamp a line of your log: submit its id to
                       OpenTimestamps calendars and commit the pending proof
                       with an anchors statement
  anchor upgrade       complete pending timestamps: ask the calendars for the
                       Bitcoin path of each pending proof and commit an upgraded
                       anchors statement
  anchor status        this reader's chain backend: provider, mode, network,
                       bootstrap, tip, last sync, freshness, receipt count
  anchor headers sync  validate Bitcoin block headers from a file and persist
                       them as this reader's chain view

Global options:
  --json         print one JSON object on stdout (an RFC 9457 problem-details
                 object on error)
  --store <dir>  the store to read (default: $COMMONS_STORE, else the nearest
                 ancestor directory holding rc-store)
  --help         print help for the command and exit 0
  --version      print the version and exit 0

More:
  commons help <command> — the options of one command
  commons help outputs — the state tokens a result can carry
  commons help exits — the exit codes
